shes` and set `_output_message_hashes` on each row.\n  - `log_row_extras` now collects results from the output parts too.\n  - Every tool call and result carries a `server_executed` key. On results it sits right after `exception`.\n  - Server results take their `parts` row id from the turn's own output messages.\n- **`llm/cli.py`:**\n  - `annotate_log_rows` strips `_output_message_hashes`.\n  - In Markdown mode the printing loop is now a nested helper, `_display_tool_results`, with unchanged output.\n  - Local results stay under the prompt's `### Tool results` heading. Server results get their own `### Tool results` block under `## Response`, after `### Tool calls` and before the response text.\n- **`docs/changelog.md`:** added the bullet under Unreleased. The spec gave the issue link in parentheses, but I followed the file's existing style and put it after a full stop, as in the bullets above it.", "ttft_ms": 1905, "type": "result", "duration_ms": 59048, "uuid": "85bd14a7-19e9-496d-80b6-8e1f7ad21a93", "ttft_stream_ms": 1419, "time_to_request_ms": 54, "first_content_frame_ms": 1419, "queued_turn_count": 0, "result_index": 0}
